From 698314e47a50c89c5467b7e89571abc1c12b7dc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:20:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0323 -- correct the stale TILEMAP_CACHE gate
 comment

The comment above the tilemap cache read:

    Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE=0 (strict-0; default ON)

Both halves are wrong. The gate is double-negated:

    _abl_tilemap_cache_killswitch() -> !_strict_truthy_env(HINT)
    unset -> killswitch ACTIVE   -> uncached per-tile loop
    ="1"  -> killswitch INACTIVE -> cache path

So =1 OPTS IN and the default is OFF. The comment was presumably true
before a default-flip and was never updated.

This is not cosmetic. A round was specified to measure the cache by
setting =1, and had that spec trusted the comment instead of the
consumer, the arm would have measured the exact inverse of its label --
and produced an internally consistent result while doing it. Two sources
agreed on the wrong answer: this comment, and a lever scan that matched
_strict_truthy_env without noticing the leading negation. Agreement
between two wrong readings is not corroboration.

What settled it was the consumer, which is now named in the comment as
the authority: `killswitch_active() || !cache_enabled || !win` selects
the uncached loop, so the branch the uncached loop sits on determines the
polarity, not the helper's name.

Also records two things found while chasing it:

`cache_enabled` is a separate adaptive-alpha condition, so the cache can
be opted in and still decline. A cell that sets the hint and sees no hits
should check that before concluding the hint did nothing.

The [mds-tilemap-cache counter is gated on MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR, not on
MDS_DECOMP. The shared `mds-` prefix does not imply a shared hint, and
assuming it did cost a cell.

Comment-only. No behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/map.cpp | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index 00020aa6..6d626ab0 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -3028,10 +3028,33 @@ void map_drawwaterlevel(void)
 // drawn beneath the FG layer (Quote, NPCs) show through correctly.
 // BG cache is opaque (full-screen coverage of plain tiles).
 //
-// Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE=0 (strict-0; default
-// ON) short-circuits the cache check entirely -- falls through to the
-// original per-tile-loop render. Counter emission still fires per
-// W22.5 hint per contract sec. 3.2.
+// Gate: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE=1 OPTS IN to the cache. Unset
+// (the default) runs the original per-tile-loop render.
+//
+// CORRECTED 2026-08-21. This comment previously read "Killswitch:
+// TILEMAP_CACHE=0 (strict-0; default ON)". Both halves were wrong, and
+// it had presumably been true before a default-flip. Read the chain
+// rather than the name before trusting either:
+//
+//   _abl_tilemap_cache_killswitch()  ->  !_strict_truthy_env(HINT)
+//   unset  -> !false = true  -> killswitch ACTIVE  -> uncached loop
+//   ="1"   -> !true  = false -> killswitch INACTIVE -> cache path
+//
+// So the helper is named for the killswitch but is really "cache not
+// enabled", and the sense is DOUBLE-NEGATED. A round that set =1
+// expecting to disable a default-ON cache would have measured the exact
+// inverse of its label and been internally consistent while doing it.
+// The consumer below (`killswitch_active() || !cache_enabled || !win`)
+// is the authority; the helper name is not.
+//
+// `cache_enabled` is a SEPARATE condition -- the adaptive-alpha state
+// `g_tilemap_*_cache_enabled` above -- so the cache can be opted in and
+// still decline for its own reasons. A cell that sets the hint and sees
+// no hits should check that before concluding the hint did nothing.
+//
+// Counter emission ([mds-tilemap-cache ...]) is gated on
+// SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR, NOT on MDS_DECOMP -- the
+// shared `mds-` prefix does not imply a shared hint.
 
 // flipacceltime is defined at global scope (in nx.cpp); declare here at
 // global scope so the anonymous-namespace `_tilemap_cache_compute_key()`
